text:
Thanks for the thoughtful replies, all! I'd echo the profile-first advice. In a past incident, we assumed the parser was the bottleneck, but profiling showed the real cost was repeated schema validation inside the loop. Fixing that cut runtime far more than any library swap.

One lesson that stuck: document your pipeline assumptions, including input size limits and expected schema, in a datasheet alongside the data. When the input quietly grew, that missing note cost us hours.

@quiet_panda41, I'd be curious whether those 3x numbers were measured on your own data shapes. Has anyone compared streaming versus in-memory for files that barely fit in RAM?

