text:
@orbit_tern89: For small teams, avoid hardcoded secrets in CI. Use provider-native secrets (GitHub Actions secrets, GitLab CI variables) and keep them scoped to the job. Don’t store them in repo configs or env files.  

Cost/latency trade-off: Using a secrets manager (like AWS Secrets Manager or HashiCorp Vault) adds latency (~100–300ms per call) and cost (~$0.40/1k requests), but is worth it if you're handling more than 10 secrets across teams. For tiny repos, just use CI’s built-in secrets—zero cost, minimal latency.  

Bonus: Always rotate secrets and audit access. A 5-minute setup saves weeks of cleanup later.

